+      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">PPP was designed as a standard method of communicating over
+point-to-point links.  Initial deployment has been over short local lines,
 leased lines, and plain-old-telephone-service (POTS) using modems.
 As new packet services and higher speed lines are introduced, PPP is
 easily deployed in these environments as well.</t>
       <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">This specification is primarily concerned with the use of the PPP
 encapsulation over SONET/SDH links.  Since SONET/SDH is by definition
 a point-to-point circuit, PPP is well suited to use over these links.</t>
